id: jf-8uuo
title: Make read-only tool-to-OpenAPI contracts exact
description: "Replace fuzzy-only agent coverage mappings for wrapper and undocumented Jellyfin routes with explicit, semantically safe contracts; expose the exact mappings through schema tools, retain truthful non-OpenAPI classifications, and verify against official stable/preview plus the owner-local read-only server."
type: Plan
status: in_progress
priority: 0
tags[7]: agents,api,coverage,openapi,read-only,tool-schema,typescript
created_at: "2026-08-09T21:35:35.900Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-09T21:42:57.928Z"
assignee: codex-jellyfin-api-20260809
author: codex-jellyfin-api-20260809
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Official stable and preview releases are refreshed from authoritative sources; Full and read-only operation coverage remain 100 percent while read-only unmatched tools fall from 8 to 0; Exact wrapper matches never select a mutating operation and appear in schema tools --openapi-match; Undocumented REST and orchestration routes are explicitly classified for agents; All source files remain below 300 LOC and strict TypeScript, lint, tests, docs, changelog, secrets, package, and read-only live gates pass"
definition_of_ready: All-status PM inventory and duplicate search complete; official/live contracts available; owner-local read-only profile validated.
goal: jf-mqpo
objective: jf-gn5j
value: Give agents deterministic API provenance instead of unsafe fuzzy guesses.
impact: Prevents read-only tools from being paired with mutating OpenAPI operations and removes false roadmap gaps.
outcome: Zero unexplained read-only tool mappings with exact contract evidence.
why_now: Live research exposed eight remaining manual mappings while repository-wide coverage is the release blocker.
parent: jf-gn5j
reviewer: maintainer
risk: high
confidence: high
sprint: jellyfin-10.11.11
